# 4-Bit Asynchronous (Ripple) Counter

## Objective
Design and simulate a 4-bit asynchronous binary counter using Verilog HDL.

## Description
A 4-bit asynchronous counter, also known as a ripple counter, consists of four flip-flops connected in series. The first flip-flop is driven by the external clock, while each subsequent flip-flop is triggered by the output of the previous flip-flop. Due to this cascading arrangement, changes ripple through the circuit, introducing a small propagation delay.

## Files

- async_counter.v
- tb_async_counter.v
- README.md

## Inputs

- clk : Clock signal
- reset : Asynchronous reset

## Outputs

- q[3:0] : 4-bit counter output

## Counting Sequence

